OL,5,T5FYELTSIN BID TO KEEP FOES IN JAIL   Tj
OL,6,T5GPresident Yeltsin tried to block   Tj
OL,7,T5Gthe release of his political foes  Tj
OL,8,T5GRuslan Khasbulatov and Alexander   Tj
OL,9,T5GRutskoi, it has been revealed.     Tj
OL,10,T5F                                   Tj
OL,11,T5FMr Yeltsin wrote to the speaker of Tj
OL,12,T5Fthe lower house of the Russian     Tj
OL,13,T5Fparliament asking him to reconsiderTj
OL,14,T5Fthe amnesty, it has emerged.       Tj
OL,15,T5F                                   Tj
OL,16,T5FAnd the Russian chief prosecutor   Tj
OL,17,T5Fsaid Mr Yeltsin asked him to       Tj
OL,18,T5Fpostpone the release of the men,   Tj
OL,19,T5Fwho led last year's failed uprisingTj
OL,20,T5F                                   Tj
OL,21,T5FGeneral Kazannik said the amnesty  Tj
OL,22,T5Fwas wrong but could not be stopped.Tj
OL,23,Tupppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppz
